NNAAMMEE
     aauuttoommoouunnttdd — daemon handling autofs mount requests

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     aauuttoommoouunnttdd [--DD _n_a_m_e_=_v_a_l_u_e] [--ii] [--mm _m_a_x_p_r_o_c] [--oo _o_p_t_i_o_n_s] [--dd] [--vv]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aauuttoommoouunnttdd daemon is responsible for handling autofs(5) mount re‐
     quests, parsing maps, and mounting filesystems they specify.  On startup,
     aauuttoommoouunnttdd forks into background and waits for kernel requests.  When a
     request is received, aauuttoommoouunnttdd forks a child process.  The child process
     parses the appropriate map and mounts filesystems accordingly.  Then it
     signals the kernel to release blocked processes that were waiting for the
     mount.

     --DD          Define a variable.

     --ii          For indirect mounts, only create subdirectories if there are
                 no wildcard entries.  Without --ii, aauuttoommoouunnttdd creates all the
                 subdirectories it can.  Users may not realize that the wild‐
                 card map entry makes it possible to access directories that
                 have not yet been created.

     --mm _m_a_x_p_r_o_c  Limit the number of forked aauuttoommoouunnttdd processes, and thus the
                 number of mount requests being handled in parallel.  The de‐
                 fault is 30.

     --dd          Debug mode: increase verbosity and do not daemonize.

     --oo _o_p_t_i_o_n_s  Specify mount options.  Options specified here will be over‐
                 ridden by options entered in maps or auto_master(5).

     --vv          Increase verbosity.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The aauuttoommoouunnttdd utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     auto_master(5), autofs(5), automount(8), autounmountd(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The aauuttoommoouunnttdd daemon appeared in FreeBSD 10.1.

